# Project Cognition Report — commander.js @ 14.0.3 snapshot

Scope: full read-only analysis of the snapshot at `D:\AI_work_project\phase-a-snapshots\commander.js\workspace` (HEAD `bf35c5f`, master, immediately after the v14.0.3 release). Analysis deliverable only; no code changes accompany it.

## 1. Project Identity

- **Project**: Commander.js — "the complete solution for node.js command-line programs". The de-facto standard CLI argument-parsing/command framework for Node.js (repo: `tj/commander.js`, npm package `commander`).
- **Snapshot version**: `14.0.3` (released 2026-01-31). HEAD commit `bf35c5f` ("Bump typescript-eslint … #2479") — the snapshot is the current release line with only dependabot churn since the tag.
- **License / stewardship**: MIT; original author TJ Holowaychuk; active maintainers shadowspawn (John Gee) and abetomo (donation-backed per `package-support.json`).
- **Runtime contract**: Node.js `>=20` (bumped in 14.0.0, aligned with Node LTS EOL policy); CommonJS package (`"type": "commonjs"`) with a thin ESM named-export wrapper (`esm.mjs`) and conditional `exports` map; hand-maintained TypeScript typings shipped (`typings/index.d.ts`, `typings/esm.d.mts`).
- **Dependency posture**: **zero production dependencies** (only `node:` built-ins: events, child_process, path, fs, process). CONTRIBUTING states zero-dependency is a near-hard requirement for accepting PRs.
- **Release policy** (`docs/release-policy.md`): semver; major ~every 6 months tied to Node LTS EOL; 14.x current, 13.x maintenance (security only) until 2026-05-18, <13 EOL.
- **Engineering stack**: Jest 30 (+ ts-jest), ESLint 9 flat config with typescript-eslint type-aware linting of both JS (via JSDoc, `tsconfig.js.json`) and TS, Prettier 3, `tsd` + `tsc` typing gates, CodeQL + GitHub Actions matrix (Node 20/22/24 × ubuntu/windows/macos).
- **Scale**: 223 tracked files; core = 6 lib modules (`command.js` 2,777 lines, `help.js` 747, `option.js` 380, `argument.js` 150, `error.js` 39, `suggestSimilar.js` 101); 109 Jest test files + 1 TS test file + ESM import test; ~45 examples (incl. extensionless executable-subcommand fixtures like `pm`, `pizza`, `deploy`); bilingual docs (English + 简体中文).

